<title>UK: OPEC Feb output 25.33 million bpd, members say.</title>
<headline>OPEC Feb output 25.33 million bpd, members say.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC pumped 25.33 million barrels per day (bpd) in February, down from a revised level of 25.36 million bpd in January, a monthly report from OPEC's Vienna-based secretariat said.</p>
<p>By comparison, a Reuters survey put OPEC output at 26.77 million bpd in February. The 11-member group has an official ceiling of 25.033 million bpd.</p>
<p>The secretariat put the likely call on OPEC crude this year at 25.30 million bpd, up 100,000 bpd from February's report.</p>
<p>According to this month's report, OPEC supply to the market in February totalled 25.22 million bpd, down from 25.27 million in January.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
